ide, and Mid-Base Gripper; picks a singulated mid-base from the Escapement's shuttle nest and places it onto the dial.\n\n## GENERATION SCOPE (contract — what this build covers vs not)\nBUILD PURPOSE (from the ME — let it shape your approach): Owns the X Axis, Z Slide, and Mid-Base Gripper; picks a singulated mid-base from the Escapement's shuttle nest and places it onto the dial.\nTHIS BUILD GENERATES: station sequence logic; servo motion commands; device commands & verification; state transitions; basic sequence faults/retries needed for the sequence.\nNOT IN THIS BUILD (machine-level extras deferred until the station joins a machine): machine-level part tracking; upstream/downstream coordination beyond defined IO; overall machine initialization; machine-wide fault manager; production/OEE logic; supervisor sequencing outside this station.\nScope law: NEVER ask about, flag, or apologize for NOT-IN-THIS-BUILD items.\nWhere the sequence touches one (e.g. a partner/supervisor signal outside the\ndefined IO), stub it quietly per the SDC standalone pattern (*Replace rung\ncomment) and move on — that is your own decision, not a question. A\nstandalone sequence terminates cleanly in \"Sequence Complete / Ready for\nnext command\".\nThe station-level template pieces ALWAYS emit regardless of scope: init\nblock, lockout, R01 inputs, station part-tracking block, alarms — the full\nstation file, never a reduced one.",
